[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m 760. Find Anagram Mappings
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m DescriptionHintsSubmissionsDiscussSolution
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m Given two lists Aand B, and B is an anagram of A. B is an anagram of A means B is made by randomizing the order of the
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m elements in A.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m We want to find an index mapping P, from A to B. A mapping P[i] = j means the ith element in A appears in B at index j.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m These lists A and B may contain duplicates. If there are multiple answers, output any of them.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m For example, given
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m A = [12, 28, 46, 32, 50]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m B = [50, 12, 32, 46, 28]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m We should return
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m [1, 4, 3, 2, 0]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m as P[0] = 1 because the 0th element of A appears at B[1], and P[1] = 4 because the 1st element of A appears at B[4],
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m and so on.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m Note:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m A, B have equal lengths in range [1, 100].
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m A[i], B[i] are integers in range [0, 10^5].
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m """
