[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m         Assumption: A and B are valid anagram to each other.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m         Basic idea:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m         loop through A and B, for every index in A, find same element in B, record it.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m         it the B's index is already used (keep record of visited), then keep searching for the next one
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m         Time: O(n ^ 2)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m         Space: O(n)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m         Idea 2:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m         1. preprocess B, keep an inverted index of B like (element: [deque of indexes])
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m         2. loop through A, find matching index list, take the first index in the 'deque of indexes', then remove the first one
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2742912)[0m         Time: O(n) + O(n * average of repeated times of an element --> not really with deque if pop used) ==> O(n)
